msgid "hydrometrics.crps"
msgstr "hydrometrics.crps"

msgid "Continuous Ranked Probability Score (CRPS)."
msgstr "Continuous Ranked Probability Score (CRPS)."

msgid "Observed values, shape (n_samples,) or (n_samples, n_stations, ...)."
msgstr "Observed values, shape (n_samples,) or (n_samples, n_stations, ...)."

msgid "Forecast values. Deterministic forecast: same shape as ``obs``; the score is the absolute error. Ensemble forecast: ``obs.shape + (n_members,)``, members on the last axis."
msgstr "Forecast values. Deterministic forecast: same shape as ``obs``; the score is the absolute error. Ensemble forecast: ``obs.shape + (n_members,)``, members on the last axis."

msgid "Ensemble forecasts only. ``False`` is the classical estimator, ``mean_j |X_j - o| - 0.5 * sum_jk |X_j - X_k| / m**2``. ``True`` is the fair estimator named in Ferro (2014), which divides the spread term by m(m - 1) instead of m**2. For m members the fair value is smaller than the classical one."
msgstr "Ensemble forecasts only. ``False`` is the classical estimator, ``mean_j |X_j - o| - 0.5 * sum_jk |X_j - X_k| / m**2``. ``True`` is the fair estimator named in Ferro (2014), which divides the spread term by m(m - 1) instead of m**2. For m members the fair value is smaller than the classical one."

msgid "*float or ndarray* -- CRPS value, in the units of ``obs``."
msgstr "*float or ndarray* -- CRPS value, in the units of ``obs``."

msgid "If the shapes of ``obs`` and ``sim`` are incompatible, a weight is negative or has the     wrong shape, ``nan_policy``, ``reduction`` or ``align`` is unknown, NaN is present with     ``nan_policy=\"raise\"``, or the labels of the inputs are not aligned (``align``).     If ``sim`` is neither shaped like ``obs`` nor ``obs.shape + (n_members,)``."
msgstr "If the shapes of ``obs`` and ``sim`` are incompatible, a weight is negative or has the     wrong shape, ``nan_policy``, ``reduction`` or ``align`` is unknown, NaN is present with     ``nan_policy=\"raise\"``, or the labels of the inputs are not aligned (``align``).     If ``sim`` is neither shaped like ``obs`` nor ``obs.shape + (n_members,)``."

msgid "Заметки"
msgstr "Notes"

msgid "Both estimators are non-negative, so ``bounds=(0, None)`` holds for ``fair=False`` and ``fair=True``: by the triangle inequality the spread term never exceeds the mean absolute error of the members. The default changed from the fair to the classical estimator."
msgstr "Both estimators are non-negative, so ``bounds=(0, None)`` holds for ``fair=False`` and ``fair=True``: by the triangle inequality the spread term never exceeds the mean absolute error of the members. The default changed from the fair to the classical estimator."

msgid "Hersbach (2000), DOI: 10.1175/1520-0434(2000)015<0559:DOTCRP>2.0.CO;2"
msgstr "Hersbach (2000), DOI: 10.1175/1520-0434(2000)015<0559:DOTCRP>2.0.CO;2"

msgid "Gneiting & Raftery (2007), DOI: 10.1198/016214506000001437"
msgstr "Gneiting & Raftery (2007), DOI: 10.1198/016214506000001437"

msgid "Ferro (2014), DOI: 10.1002/qj.2270"
msgstr "Ferro (2014), DOI: 10.1002/qj.2270"

msgid "hydrometrics.crpss"
msgstr "hydrometrics.crpss"

msgid "Continuous Ranked Probability Skill Score (CRPSS)."
msgstr "Continuous Ranked Probability Skill Score (CRPSS)."

msgid "CRPSS = 1 - mean(CRPS) / mean(CRPS_ref): the ratio of the means over ``axis``, not the mean of per-observation ratios. Both scores use the classical estimator of :func:`crps`."
msgstr "CRPSS = 1 - mean(CRPS) / mean(CRPS_ref): the ratio of the means over ``axis``, not the mean of per-observation ratios. Both scores use the classical estimator of :func:`crps`."

msgid "Forecast values: same shape as ``obs`` or ``obs.shape + (n_members,)``."
msgstr "Forecast values: same shape as ``obs`` or ``obs.shape + (n_members,)``."

msgid "Reference forecast for skill score, deterministic or an ensemble. If None, the (weighted) mean of the observations is the deterministic reference."
msgstr "Reference forecast for skill score, deterministic or an ensemble. If None, the (weighted) mean of the observations is the deterministic reference."

msgid "*float or ndarray* -- CRPSS value."
msgstr "*float or ndarray* -- CRPSS value."

msgid "hydrometrics.edi"
msgstr "hydrometrics.edi"

msgid "Extremal Dependence Index (EDI)."
msgstr "Extremal Dependence Index (EDI)."

msgid "True binary labels (0 or 1)."
msgstr "True binary labels (0 or 1)."

msgid "Predicted binary labels (0 or 1)."
msgstr "Predicted binary labels (0 or 1)."

msgid "*float or ndarray* -- EDI value in [-1, 1]."
msgstr "*float or ndarray* -- EDI value in [-1, 1]."

msgid "H = TP / (TP + FN)  -- hit rate F = FP / (FP + TN)  -- false alarm rate EDI = (log F - log H) / (log F + log H)"
msgstr "H = TP / (TP + FN)  -- hit rate F = FP / (FP + TN)  -- false alarm rate EDI = (log F - log H) / (log F + log H)"

msgid "A perfect forecast (H = 1 and F = 0) is defined to give 1. In the other cases with H = 0 or F = 0 the result is NaN, because a logarithm of 0 appears. For H = 1 and 0 < F < 1, log H = 0 and EDI equals 1. The definition at H = 1, F = 0 is a decision of the library author; the source text could not be checked. Pairs with a missing value count in none of the four cells."
msgstr "A perfect forecast (H = 1 and F = 0) is defined to give 1. In the other cases with H = 0 or F = 0 the result is NaN, because a logarithm of 0 appears. For H = 1 and 0 < F < 1, log H = 0 and EDI equals 1. The definition at H = 1, F = 0 is a decision of the library author; the source text could not be checked. Pairs with a missing value count in none of the four cells."

