msgid "Forecast verification criterion for hydrological forecasts."
msgstr "Forecast verification criterion for hydrological forecasts."

msgid "A forecast is considered verified when its absolute error is less than 0.674 times the sample standard deviation (``ddof=1``) of all observations along ``axis``. The coefficient is the module constant ``PROBABLE_ERROR_COEFFICIENT`` of ``hydrometrics.backends.numpy``, the probable deviation of the normal law (0.6745 sigma)."
msgstr "A forecast is considered verified when its absolute error is less than 0.674 times the sample standard deviation (``ddof=1``) of all observations along ``axis``. The coefficient is the module constant ``PROBABLE_ERROR_COEFFICIENT`` of ``hydrometrics.backends.numpy``, the probable deviation of the normal law (0.6745 sigma)."

msgid "Forecast or simulated values."
msgstr "Forecast or simulated values."

msgid "Not supported by this metric: a weight (or its alias ``weight``) raises ``NotImplementedError``."
msgstr "Not supported by this metric: a weight (or its alias ``weight``) raises ``NotImplementedError``."

msgid "*float or np.ndarray* -- With ``reduction=\"mean\"``, the fraction of verified forecasts. With ``reduction=\"none\"``, an array of 1.0 (verified), 0.0 (not verified) and NaN where the error or the threshold is undefined, for example for a missing observation or forecast."
msgstr "*float or np.ndarray* -- With ``reduction=\"mean\"``, the fraction of verified forecasts. With ``reduction=\"none\"``, an array of 1.0 (verified), 0.0 (not verified) and NaN where the error or the threshold is undefined, for example for a missing observation or forecast."

msgid "Georgievsky, Y. M., & Shanochkin, S. V. (2007). Hydrological Forecasts."
msgstr "Georgievsky, Y. M., & Shanochkin, S. V. (2007). Hydrological Forecasts."

msgid "hydrometrics.forecast\\_verification\\_delta"
msgstr "hydrometrics.forecast\\_verification\\_delta"

msgid "Calculate the forecast verification criterion based on forecast errors."
msgstr "Calculate the forecast verification criterion based on forecast errors."

msgid "For each reference date, the sample standard deviation (``ddof=1``) of the forecast errors ``sim - obs`` is calculated across valid pairs. A forecast is considered verified if its absolute error is less than 0.674 times this standard deviation (``PROBABLE_ERROR_COEFFICIENT`` of ``hydrometrics.backends.numpy``)."
msgstr "For each reference date, the sample standard deviation (``ddof=1``) of the forecast errors ``sim - obs`` is calculated across valid pairs. A forecast is considered verified if its absolute error is less than 0.674 times this standard deviation (``PROBABLE_ERROR_COEFFICIENT`` of ``hydrometrics.backends.numpy``)."

msgid "Here sigma_delta is the spread of the forecast errors ``sim - obs`` within a reference-date group."
msgstr "Here sigma_delta is the spread of the forecast errors ``sim - obs`` within a reference-date group."

msgid "Simulated or forecast values."
msgstr "Simulated or forecast values."

