msgid "Reliability (calibration) term of the Brier score decomposition of Murphy (1973): sum_k n_k / n * (mean(p_k) - mean(o_k))^2."
msgstr "Reliability (calibration) term of the Brier score decomposition of Murphy (1973): sum_k n_k / n * (mean(p_k) - mean(o_k))^2."

msgid "The forecast probabilities are grouped into ``n_bins`` equal-width bins on [0, 1]. Bins are half-open, [a, b); the last bin is closed on the right, so a probability of exactly 1 is counted. With weights, n_k and n are sums of weights and the bin means of the probability and of the frequency are weighted means. The resolution and uncertainty terms are not computed. A ``ValueError`` is raised if ``obs`` holds a value other than 0 or 1, if ``sim`` lies outside [0, 1] or if ``n_bins`` is not an integer of at least 1."
msgstr "The forecast probabilities are grouped into ``n_bins`` equal-width bins on [0, 1]. Bins are half-open, [a, b); the last bin is closed on the right, so a probability of exactly 1 is counted. With weights, n_k and n are sums of weights and the bin means of the probability and of the frequency are weighted means. The resolution and uncertainty terms are not computed. A ``ValueError`` is raised if ``obs`` holds a value other than 0 or 1, if ``sim`` lies outside [0, 1] or if ``n_bins`` is not an integer of at least 1."

