msgstr "Gneiting & Ranjan (2011), DOI: 10.1198/jbes.2010.08110"

msgid "hydrometrics.willmott\\_d"
msgstr "hydrometrics.willmott\\_d"

msgid "Willmott's Index of Agreement (d)."
msgstr "Willmott's Index of Agreement (d)."

msgid "Implements the original index of Willmott (1981), ``d = 1 - sum((O - P)^2) / sum((|P - mean(O)| + |O - mean(O)|)^2)``. With weights, the sums and the observed mean are weighted. Modified and refined variants of the index, including the refined index of Willmott et al. (2012), are not implemented."
msgstr "Implements the original index of Willmott (1981), ``d = 1 - sum((O - P)^2) / sum((|P - mean(O)| + |O - mean(O)|)^2)``. With weights, the sums and the observed mean are weighted. Modified and refined variants of the index, including the refined index of Willmott et al. (2012), are not implemented."

msgid "*float or ndarray* -- Willmott's d value."
msgstr "*float or ndarray* -- Willmott's d value."

msgid "Willmott (1981), DOI: 10.1080/02723646.1981.10642213"
msgstr "Willmott (1981), DOI: 10.1080/02723646.1981.10642213"

msgid "Willmott et al. (2012), DOI: 10.1002/joc.2419"
msgstr "Willmott et al. (2012), DOI: 10.1002/joc.2419"

msgid "Вспомогательные функции и реестр"
msgstr "Helper functions and the registry"

msgid "Из ``hydrometrics`` экспортируются три объекта, которые не являются метриками: две функции для построения режимных кривых и реестр, через который вызов метрики попадает на нужный бэкенд."
msgstr "``hydrometrics`` exports three objects that are not metrics: two functions that build regime curves and the registry through which a metric call reaches the right backend."

msgid "Средний годовой гидрограф"
msgstr "Mean annual hydrograph"

msgid "Функция :func:`~hydrometrics.mean_annual_hydrograph` усредняет значения по календарным суткам за все годы ряда; пропуски не учитываются. Если в ряду есть високосный год, результат содержит 366 значений, и 29 февраля занимает отдельное место."
msgstr "The function :func:`~hydrometrics.mean_annual_hydrograph` averages the values by calendar day over all years of the series; gaps are ignored. If the series contains a leap year, the result has 366 values and 29 February keeps a place of its own."

msgid "Функция :func:`~hydrometrics.mean_annual_hydrograph_duration_curve` сортирует средний годовой гидрограф по убыванию. Из 366 значений получается 365: при наличии високосного года усредняются два наименьших значения, то есть значения на 365-й и 366-й позициях ранжированного ряда (то же правило, что для годовых кривых в :ref:`metric-regNSE`). Это позиции по рангу, а не календарные дни. Полученная кривая служит опорной в :ref:`metric-regNSE`."
msgstr "The function :func:`~hydrometrics.mean_annual_hydrograph_duration_curve` sorts the mean annual hydrograph in descending order. 366 values are reduced to 365 when a leap year is present by averaging the two smallest values, that is the values at positions 365 and 366 of the ranked series (the same rule as for the annual curves in :ref:`metric-regNSE`). These are rank positions, not calendar days. The resulting curve is the reference of :ref:`metric-regNSE`."

msgid "Compute mean annual hydrograph."
msgstr "Compute mean annual hydrograph."

msgid "Returns 366 values if the input series contains any leap year, otherwise 365 values. 29 February is kept as its own calendar day."
msgstr "Returns 366 values if the input series contains any leap year, otherwise 365 values. 29 February is kept as its own calendar day."

msgid "Observed discharge values, one-dimensional."
msgstr "Observed discharge values, one-dimensional."

msgid "Observation dates, same shape as ``obs``."
msgstr "Observation dates, same shape as ``obs``."

msgid "*np.ndarray* -- Mean discharge for each calendar day (365 or 366 values)."
msgstr "*np.ndarray* -- Mean discharge for each calendar day (365 or 366 values)."

msgid "Compute a flow duration curve based on the mean annual hydrograph."
msgstr "Compute a flow duration curve based on the mean annual hydrograph."

msgid "Compute the mean annual hydrograph (365 or 366 values)."
msgstr "Compute the mean annual hydrograph (365 or 366 values)."

msgid "Sort it in descending order."
msgstr "Sort it in descending order."

msgid "If the result has 366 values, average the values at ranks 365 and 366 of the descending ranking (the two smallest) so that the final length is 365. These are rank positions, not calendar days: after sorting, 29 February has no fixed position. The annual curves of ``regNSE`` follow the same rule."
msgstr "If the result has 366 values, average the values at ranks 365 and 366 of the descending ranking (the two smallest) so that the final length is 365. These are rank positions, not calendar days: after sorting, 29 February has no fixed position. The annual curves of ``regNSE`` follow the same rule."

msgid "Observed discharge values."
msgstr "Observed discharge values."

msgid "Observation dates."
msgstr "Observation dates."

msgid "*np.ndarray* -- Flow duration curve with 365 values, sorted in descending order."
msgstr "*np.ndarray* -- Flow duration curve with 365 values, sorted in descending order."

msgid "Пример: два водных года с половодьем в конце апреля, расход в м³/с."
msgstr "Example: two water years with a spring flood in late April, discharge in m³/s."

msgid ""
"import numpy as np\n"
"import hydrometrics as hm\n"
"\n"
"dates = np.arange(\"2011-10-01\", \"2013-10-01\", dtype=\"datetime64[D]\")  # contains 29 February 2012\n"
"doy = (dates - dates.astype(\"datetime64[Y]\")).astype(int)\n"
"q = 20 + 150 * np.exp(-(((doy - 118) / 16.0) ** 2))  # synthetic flood hydrograph, m3/s\n"
"hydrograph = hm.mean_annual_hydrograph(q, dates)\n"
"curve = hm.mean_annual_hydrograph_duration_curve(q, dates)\n"
"print(hydrograph.shape, curve.shape)\n"
"print(bool(np.all(np.diff(curve) <= 0)), round(float(curve[0]), 1), round(float(curve[-1]), 1))"
msgstr ""
"import numpy as np\n"
"import hydrometrics as hm\n"
"\n"
"dates = np.arange(\"2011-10-01\", \"2013-10-01\", dtype=\"datetime64[D]\")  # contains 29 February 2012\n"
"doy = (dates - dates.astype(\"datetime64[Y]\")).astype(int)\n"
"q = 20 + 150 * np.exp(-(((doy - 118) / 16.0) ** 2))  # synthetic flood hydrograph, m3/s\n"
"hydrograph = hm.mean_annual_hydrograph(q, dates)\n"
"curve = hm.mean_annual_hydrograph_duration_curve(q, dates)\n"
"print(hydrograph.shape, curve.shape)\n"
"print(bool(np.all(np.diff(curve) <= 0)), round(float(curve[0]), 1), round(float(curve[-1]), 1))"

