"True 170.0 20.0"

msgid "Реестр бэкендов"
msgstr "Backend registry"

msgid "Каждая метрика зарегистрирована в реестре под своим именем для numpy, pandas, polars и xarray. Публичная функция, например ``hydrometrics.nse``, это диспетчер: он смотрит на тип входов и вызывает реализацию нужного бэкенда, а при её отсутствии реализацию numpy. Глобальный реестр доступен как ``hydrometrics.registry``."
msgstr "Every metric is registered under its name for NumPy, pandas, polars and xarray. A public function such as ``hydrometrics.nse`` is a dispatcher: it looks at the type of the inputs and calls the implementation of that backend, or the NumPy one if there is none. The global registry is available as ``hydrometrics.registry``."

msgid ""
"import hydrometrics as hm\n"
"\n"
"print(type(hm.registry).__name__)\n"
"print(hm.registry.get_dispatcher(\"nse\").__name__)"
msgstr ""
"import hydrometrics as hm\n"
"\n"
"print(type(hm.registry).__name__)\n"
"print(hm.registry.get_dispatcher(\"nse\").__name__)"

msgid ""
"BackendRegistry\n"
"nse"
msgstr ""
"BackendRegistry\n"
"nse"

msgid "Собственную метрику создаёт декоратор :func:`hydrometrics.core.base.metric`; регистрация в реестре даёт ей единый вызов со всеми параметрами метрик пакета (``nan_policy``, ``sample_weight``, ``axis``, ``reduction``). В примере используется отдельный экземпляр реестра, чтобы не менять глобальный."
msgstr "A custom metric is made with the decorator :func:`hydrometrics.core.base.metric`; registering it gives it the unified call with all the parameters of the package metrics (``nan_policy``, ``sample_weight``, ``axis``, ``reduction``). The example uses a separate registry instance so as not to change the global one."

msgid ""
"import numpy as np\n"
"import pandas as pd\n"
"from hydrometrics.core.base import metric\n"
"from hydrometrics.core.dispatch import BackendRegistry\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"@metric(name=\"Mean ratio\", direction=\"target\", bounds=(0.0, None), reference=\"own\", optimum=1.0)\n"
"def mean_ratio(obs, sim, *, weight=None, axis=None, reduction=\"mean\"):\n"
"    \"\"\"Ratio of the means of simulated and observed values.\"\"\"\n"
"    return np.nanmean(sim, axis=axis) / np.nanmean(obs, axis=axis)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"registry = BackendRegistry()  # a private registry; hydrometrics.registry holds the package metrics\n"
"registry.register_numpy(\"mean_ratio\", mean_ratio)\n"
"dispatch = registry.get_dispatcher(\"mean_ratio\")\n"
"\n"
"q_obs = pd.Series([10.0, 20.0, np.nan, 40.0])\n"
"q_sim = pd.Series([12.0, 18.0, 25.0, 44.0])\n"
"result = dispatch(q_obs, q_sim)\n"
"print(round(float(result), 4), result.direction, result.nan_info[\"n_nan_removed\"])"
msgstr ""
"import numpy as np\n"
"import pandas as pd\n"
"from hydrometrics.core.base import metric\n"
"from hydrometrics.core.dispatch import BackendRegistry\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"@metric(name=\"Mean ratio\", direction=\"target\", bounds=(0.0, None), reference=\"own\", optimum=1.0)\n"
"def mean_ratio(obs, sim, *, weight=None, axis=None, reduction=\"mean\"):\n"
"    \"\"\"Ratio of the means of simulated and observed values.\"\"\"\n"
"    return np.nanmean(sim, axis=axis) / np.nanmean(obs, axis=axis)\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"registry = BackendRegistry()  # a private registry; hydrometrics.registry holds the package metrics\n"
"registry.register_numpy(\"mean_ratio\", mean_ratio)\n"
"dispatch = registry.get_dispatcher(\"mean_ratio\")\n"
"\n"
"q_obs = pd.Series([10.0, 20.0, np.nan, 40.0])\n"
"q_sim = pd.Series([12.0, 18.0, 25.0, 44.0])\n"
"result = dispatch(q_obs, q_sim)\n"
"print(round(float(result), 4), result.direction, result.nan_info[\"n_nan_removed\"])"

msgid "1.0571 target 1"
msgstr "1.0571 target 1"

msgid "Для pandas-входа в этом примере нет отдельной реализации, поэтому используется numpy-функция; пара с пропуском удалена, а число удалённых пар записано в ``nan_info``."
msgstr "There is no pandas-specific implementation in this example, so the NumPy function is used; the pair with a gap is dropped and the number of dropped pairs is recorded in ``nan_info``."

msgid "Registry of metric functions, one implementation per backend."
msgstr "Registry of metric functions, one implementation per backend."

msgid "Each metric is registered under a name for the backends it supports (``register_numpy``, ``register_pandas``, ``register_polars``, ``register_xarray``). ``get_dispatcher`` returns a function that looks at the type of its inputs and calls the implementation of that backend, falling back to the NumPy one when a backend has none. The package registers all of its metrics in the global instance ``hydrometrics.registry``; a new metric made with :func:`hydrometrics.core.base.metric` can be registered the same way."
msgstr "Each metric is registered under a name for the backends it supports (``register_numpy``, ``register_pandas``, ``register_polars``, ``register_xarray``). ``get_dispatcher`` returns a function that looks at the type of its inputs and calls the implementation of that backend, falling back to the NumPy one when a backend has none. The package registers all of its metrics in the global instance ``hydrometrics.registry``; a new metric made with :func:`hydrometrics.core.base.metric` can be registered the same way."

msgid "Register the NumPy implementation of metric ``name`` (also the fallback for the others)."
msgstr "Register the NumPy implementation of metric ``name`` (also the fallback for the others)."

msgid "Register the implementation used for pandas ``Series`` and ``DataFrame`` inputs."
msgstr "Register the implementation used for pandas ``Series`` and ``DataFrame`` inputs."

msgid "Register the implementation used for xarray ``DataArray`` and ``Dataset`` inputs."
msgstr "Register the implementation used for xarray ``DataArray`` and ``Dataset`` inputs."

msgid "Register the implementation used for polars ``Series`` and ``DataFrame`` inputs."
msgstr "Register the implementation used for polars ``Series`` and ``DataFrame`` inputs."

msgid "Create a dispatching function for a given metric name."
msgstr "Create a dispatching function for a given metric name."

msgid "The function takes ``(obs, sim, **kwargs)``, chooses the backend from the input types (xarray, then pandas, then polars, otherwise NumPy) and calls its implementation. The name, docstring, signature and metadata attributes are copied from the NumPy implementation, which must be registered."
msgstr "The function takes ``(obs, sim, **kwargs)``, chooses the backend from the input types (xarray, then pandas, then polars, otherwise NumPy) and calls its implementation. The name, docstring, signature and metadata attributes are copied from the NumPy implementation, which must be registered."

